    "explanation": "Summary for both parties: the 5.00 SGD no-show fee was correctly reversed, and because the driver filed this dispute, the present state stands. Nothing moves in either direction.\n\nWhat is not in dispute. The driver arrived at the pickup (Block 210, Tampines Street 23) at 10:17:00, and the GPS trace corroborates it: the nearest fix is 5.75 m from the pickup at 10:17:11 with a reported accuracy of 4 m, inside the STANDARD arrival radius of 50 m and inside the 25 m accuracy filter. He then observed the full 300-second free wait, which expired at 10:22:00, and did not cancel until 10:23:30 — 390 seconds after arrival, with cancelled_after_free_wait true. The arrival and the wait satisfy POL-NS-21, and the fee on the record is exactly the policy's 5.00 SGD (fee_matches_policy true), so POL-NS-22's fee-amount check does not fire.\n\nWhy the charge still fails. POL-NS-23 (v2.1 2.3) requires the driver, before cancelling for a no-show, to have sent at least one in-app chat message AND placed at least one in-app call, both before the cancellation. The message limb is met — two messages sent at 10:17:20 and 10:20:45, both before 10:23:30. The call limb is not: the trip record's in-app call list is empty (call_count 0), there is no voice-call entry in the chat log, and the derived contact block records obligation_met false. The driver's filing says he 'called the passenger two times', but nothing in the record supports it and the driver's own submissions do not press it. Where either limb is missing, POL-NS-23 voids the fee and the rider is not charged, with no driver compensation. POL-NS-22 cannot rescue the charge, because its entitlement to the 5.00 SGD presupposes a fee that stands, and on this record none does.\n\nThe money. EV-FARE-05062 shows a 5.00 SGD cancellation fee, total_charged 5.00 SGD, refund_issued_sgd 5.00 SGD and payment_status REFUNDED, and the trip record shows the fee_reversed event at 11:56:30 that returned the 5.00 SGD to the rider and withheld it from the driver. The rider is owed that refund, so your claim fails, driver, and the present state stands: NO_ACTION, with both amount fields null.\n\nThe remaining points. The read receipts do not change anything — even taken at their strongest against the rider (read at 10:17:33 and 10:21:22), the limb that failed is the call, not the reading of a message. That the reversal was logged 'pending review' only means this is the first decision on the merits, which are as set out above. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05062-01 is missing (weight 0.0) and, under POL-GEN-02(3), carries no fact; it bears on neither the contact obligation nor the timing of the wait, and no fact this decision needs is left unestablished, so POL-GEN-26 is not engaged. No fraud flag is present on either profile and the amount contested is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so per POL-NS-26 this AI ruling is final.\n\nReferrals: none. The fee charged is exactly 5.00 SGD, so the POL-NS-22 amount-check referral does not fire; the rider profile does not carry the no_show_cancellations_30d counter that POL-NS-25 requires (the rule applies only when that field is present); and POL-NS-24's 5.00 SGD goodwill credit is a remedy for a driver no-show, which did not happen here because the driver arrived.",
