    "explanation": "To the driver: your claim for the 5.00 SGD no-show fee fails, and nothing is returned to you. POL-NS-23 required that, before cancelling for a no-show, you both sent at least one in-app message AND placed at least one in-app call to the rider, each before the 10:23:30 cancellation. The chat log (EV-CHAT-05062) shows your two messages (10:17:20 and 10:20:45), but the trip record (EV-TRIP-05062) records no in-app calls at all (in_app_calls empty; call_count 0; obligation_met false) and the chat log contains no voice-call entry, so the call limb was never performed — a point your own advocate expressly accepted rather than pressed. Because the obligation is conjunctive, one missing limb voids the fee 'with no driver compensation'. Arriving and waiting do not cure it: the trip record and the GPS trace (EV-GPS-05062) corroborate your 10:17:00 arrival (nearest fix 5.75 m from the pickup at 10:17:11, accuracy 4 m, inside the 50 m STANDARD radius) and your 390 s wait past the 300 s free wait, but POL-NS-21 permits a no-show cancellation and POL-NS-22 charges the fee only when the contact obligation is also met. Your remaining points do not change this: read receipts (10:17:33, 10:21:22) cannot supply a missing call, and the fact that the 11:56:30 reversal followed a complaint rather than a finding is met by deciding the merits here and now, on this record. To the rider: you keep the 5.00 SGD already refunded. EV-FARE-05062 shows 5.00 charged and refund_issued_sgd 5.00 with payment_status REFUNDED, and the trip record logs the fee_reversed event at 2026-09-02T11:56:30 refunding you and withholding the amount from the driver; that state stands. Your account that the driver never called matches the platform's own call list, but the deciding fact rests on the full-weight records and does not need your statement. Because the driver filed this dispute against a refund already issued and recovered, his unsupported claim leaves the present state standing: NO_ACTION, with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both null. No referral arises — the fee charged is exactly the 5.00 SGD schedule figure, so POL-NS-22's amount check is not engaged; the driver did attempt contact, so POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not arise; and rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d is not carried on this record, so POL-NS-25's repeat no-show flag does not fire. The one incomplete artifact, EV-ADVIS-05062-01 (status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), carries no fact bearing on contact or timing and changes nothing. No fraud flag is present and the 5.00 SGD value sits below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so POL-NS-26 makes this ruling final. Confidence 0.95, capped by the weight-1.0 records (EV-TRIP-05062, EV-CHAT-05062) that carry the deciding fact."
